# Bruriah verifies bundled skill packs by digest. A checkout that rewrites line endings changes
# those bytes and the registry fails closed with `registry_load_failed:digest_mismatch` -- which
# reads as a corrupt install, not as a misconfigured Git. Windows clones default to
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file the packaged product is broken on checkout, before
# any code runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Digest-verified payloads and their manifests are bytes, not text. Never let any platform,
# attribute inheritance, or user config touch them.
src/bruriah/data/** -text
